      "problem": "$(4+\\text{i})(1+5\\,\\text{i})=$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying two complex numbers is similar to multiplying two binomials. We also use the fact that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+\\text{i})(1+5\\,\\text{i}) & =4\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 5\\,\\text{i}+\\text{i}\\cdot 1+\\text{i}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =4+20\\,\\text{i}+\\text{i}+5\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =4+21\\,\\text{i}+5\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+21\\,\\text{i}-5 \\\\  & =-1+21\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
